ind, wie Sie uns kontaktieren können und wie wir personenbezogene Daten verarbeiten. Bitte geben Sie Ihre Einwilligungs-ID und das Datum an, wenn Sie uns bezüglich Ihrer Einwilligung kontaktieren. Meine persönlichen Daten nicht verkaufen oder weitergeben Ablehnen Auswahl erlauben Anpassen Alle zulassen Jobs Alle Jobs anzeigen Events Alle Veranstaltungen anzeigen Student Services Arbeitgeberprofile Corporate Services LNOC Für Studierende Für Arbeitgeber LNOC Manual - Infos für Arbeitgeber JobHub Für Studierende Für Arbeitgeber Login DE Deutsch English WHO: Programme Budget Analyst (JPO, P2), Geneva cinfo 100% Feststelle - Berufserfahrene Schweiz - Westschweiz & Wallis JPO Swiss JPO Programme United Nations multilateral organisations SDC Beschreibung Facebook Twitter LinkedIn New Junior Professional Officer (JPO) position Qualified Swiss professionals with at least 3 year’s relevant experience are invited to submit their applications for the following position: WHO: Programme Budget Analyst (JPO, P2), Geneva Part of the Swiss JPO Programme , this position is sponsored by the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation SDC. This position is reserved for Swiss nationals holding a Master’s degree and strong interest in a career in multilateral organizations (max. age: 32 years). Application deadline: 20 September 2026 For more information click here of 4 100% Rotate Clockwise Rotate Counterclockwise Switch Orientation First Page Last Page Reset Zoom Print Document Download Document View Metadata Draw Junior Professional Officer Assignment and Candidate Profile Form PART I: INFORMATION ABOUT THE ASSIGNMENT Title : Programme Budget Analyst Grade: P - 2 Duty Station: Geneva, Switzerland Contract type: Fixed - term appointment (JPO) Programme/Department : Budget Coordination and Grant Management unit, Department of Planning, resource Coordination and Performance Monitoring Duration: 2 to 3 year assignment : 1 - year fixed - term appointment renewable up to 3 years subject to satisfactory performance. Extension for 3rd year will depend on availability of financial resources and the candidate’s performance. Possibility of 1 re - assignment to a different office or duty station, if of interest to the JPO and depending on availabili ty of funds. Objective of the WHO Programme /Department: The Budget Coordination and Grant Management Unit is one of two units in the Department of Planning, Resource Coordination , Performance Monitoring and Grants Management (PRP). PRP's mandate is to enable the implementation of an efficient and effective results - based management framework in support of WHO's global health mandate through the development of Organization - wide policies, systems, tools and services. The Budget Coordination and Grant Management Unit focuse s on development and management of the Programme budget, manages end - to - end grant management process and coordinates effective resource allocation efforts across WHO, taking a unified budget and results - based approach. It deals with WHO - wide agreements and works closely with the Comptroller, Directors of Administration and Finance, Assistant Directors - General in HQ and Directors of Programme Management in regional offices, to: 1) develop a long - term strategic approach to guarantee adequate distribution of financial resources for the Organization; 2) coordinate projected resource requirements and gaps Organization - wide; 3 ) ensure the strategic and optimal use of different sources of funds; 4) ensure a more consistent and coherent organi zational approach to the full grant management cycle from conception to completion to further improve WHO’s credibility, transparency and efficiency. It is responsible for production of reports for different audiences for resource allocation and budgeting purposes. Assignment Summary : As part of the Budget Coordination and Grant Management (BCG) team and broader department of Planning, Resource Coordination , Performance Monitoring and Grants Management (PRP), and under the overall supervision of the BCG Unit Head, the Junior Professional Officer ( JPO ) will support the enhancement and regular update of the WHO Programme budget web portal; contribute to the advancement of efficiency agenda; participate in the strategic budget development and presentation; support regular budget reviews and review of the HQ HR plan implementation ; work closely with regional programme management counterparts and HQ teams and divisions . Stelle anzeigen Publikationsdatum 10.09.2026 Arbeitspensum (%) 100% Branche NGO / NPO / Verbände Funktionsbereich Rechnungswesen & Controlling Stellenantritt Nach Vereinbarung Arbeitsort Eigerstrasse 57 3007 Bern Schweiz Kontaktinformationen Frau Recruitment Team E-Mail Eigerstrasse 57 3007 Bern Unsere Partner Unser Partner in Stilfragen Unser Partner für Karrierethemen Kontakt UZH Universität Zürich Career Services der Universität Zürich Schönberggasse 15 8001 Zürich info@careerservices.uzh.ch Studierende: +41 44 634 59 80 Arbeitgeber: +41 44 634 21 62 Nützliche Links FAQ Datenschutzerklärung AGB Über uns Doppelt profitieren mit nur einem Profil! Mit deinem uzhcareer-Login hast du auch Zugriff auf uzhstudy.ch. Hier gehts zu uzhstudy.ch Social Media"
